## What I changed and why

The old page buried the one thing a patient actually opens it for. The redesign reorders the page around three questions in the order they get asked: *Can I be seen today? What does it cost? How do I get there?*

**The status card is now the centerpiece.** Instead of a hardcoded sentence in a thin green strip, `getWalkInStatus()` (`src/App.jsx:98`) derives the answer from the clock against the real hours table, with four honest states: open, opens-later-today, registration-closed-but-still-open, and closed. It sits in the hero as a sticky card with a colour-coded dot, today's hours, "Cost of a visit — Free", and a link to the full table. I verified all four branches against Mon/Fri/Sat/Sun edge times, including the 19:30 cutoff and the "come in anyway if urgent" case.

**Cost is now scannable per service.** Each of the six services carries a "Walk in today" / "Appointment needed" pill at the top — the distinction that decides whether someone gets on a bus right now — and eligibility and cost are labelled rows so you can read down one column across the whole grid.

**The address and phone got treated as the destination they are.** A dark green card at 24–26px type, phone as a tap target, transit options as separate icon rows rather than a bullet list — a bus rider and a driver can each find their own line.

**Assurances kept prominent.** The three "no insurance / no immigration questions / no cost" claims are now shield-marked chips directly under the headline, above the fold.

**Emergency notice strengthened.** Moved to a solid red full-bleed bar at the very top, lead with the symptoms rather than the conditional, and added a tap-to-call 911 button.

Also: a fixed bottom Call/Directions bar on phones, today's row highlighted in the hours table, 17px base type with generous touch targets, visible focus rings, and `prefers-reduced-motion` respected.

Every preserved item is intact — full hours table, all six services with their exact eligibility and cost strings, address, both phone numbers, all seven languages, interpreter line, and the 911 notice.
